35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the rain data is clear: the eaves are dry, but the rest is soaked. Does the station park cost justify moving everyone there?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the station park is 2,600 yen monthly with a fourteen-household waitlist. It’s not a viable alternative for us.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: @Mio, the sticker register shows daily riders would rather pay than be treated as equal. Does that support a paid system?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, willingness to pay doesn’t mean a paid system works. The neighbor’s block had arrears and people stopped showing up.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@George, the daily riders’ preference is noted, but the display frame took twenty seconds and two hands to load. That’s a physical barrier for many.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, twenty seconds is manageable, but the rain exposure is not. If we use open racks, the wet spots will still cause damage and complaints.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, twenty seconds is trivial compared to the administrative burden. The ledger shows capital work requires a levy, and the station park is full. We can’t outsource this.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the ledger confirms capital work needs a levy, but the sticker register shows daily riders prefer paying. That suggests a paid model might actually be accepted.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, acceptance is fragile. The neighbor’s block shows arrears lead to social withdrawal. We risk turning neighbors into debtors, not just users.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I hear you, but the ledger shows three hours monthly just for current collections. Adding per-place billing on top of that is a recipe for burnout, not just debt.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, burnout is a risk, but the rain data is undeniable. If we don’t protect the bikes, the complaints will drown out any administrative concerns.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the rain is a maintenance issue, not a financial one. I need to know if the ledger covers that upkeep, or if we’re just shifting the cost to the residents.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the minutes show the same flats held covered spots for years without review. That’s the real cost: entrenched privilege, not just rain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, entrenched privilege is a symptom of bad rules, not a reason to ignore the social fallout. If we break the trust, we lose the community.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I agree, but if the racks are too heavy to use, people will just abandon them anyway.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
