60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the station park is full and expensive. We must solve the rain and morning chaos here. What is your cost estimate for a proper covered solution?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ledger shows capital work requires a levy. I can’t give a number without a quote, but the station park is a dead end.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Asuka, the minutes prove the current setup is stagnant. We need a system that actually rotates access, not just a more expensive version of the same problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, rotation is easy to say. The neighbor’s block shows that when rules bite, people stop showing up. I need to know how we prevent that social collapse.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, the neighbor’s block failed because billing was added to existing chaos. If we simplify the physical setup, the administrative load drops, and people stay engaged.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, simplifying the physical setup ignores the rain. If bikes are soaked, complaints will rise regardless of how easy the racks are to use.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, rain is a maintenance cost, not a reason to ignore the ledger. If we can’t afford the capital levy, we can’t afford the racks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the sticker register shows daily riders prefer paying. If we implement a paid system, we address the cost and the hoarding simultaneously.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, the neighbor’s block proves that charging people for space creates debtors, not neighbors. I won’t support a system that turns our lobby into a collection agency.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, I agree the riders want to pay, but the handover file shows three hours monthly just for current collections. Adding per-place billing on top of that is a recipe for burnout, not just debt.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the rain is a physical reality, not a budget line. If we ignore the wet spots, the complaints will drown out any administrative savings you’re promising.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ledger shows capital work requires a levy. If we can’t afford the infrastructure, we can’t afford the solution. We need a plan that fits our actual budget.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the ledger shows the money, but the minutes show the rot. We need a system that actually rotates access, not just a more expensive version of the same problem.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, rotation without enforcement is just chaos with a new name. The neighbor’s block shows that when rules bite, people stop showing up. I need to know how we prevent that social collapse.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, the neighbor’s block failed because billing was added to existing chaos. If we simplify the physical setup, the administrative load drops, and people stay engaged.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"I’m voting for Shared Racks. The rain is a maintenance issue, not a reason to keep the same stagnant, unfair allocation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I’m voting for Paid Allocation. The ledger shows we need the income, and the riders explicitly prefer paying over equal claims.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I’m voting for Annual Lottery. The minutes prove the current system is stagnant and unfair. A yearly draw resets the privilege without the social damage of charging neighbors.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I’m voting for Shared Racks. The neighbor’s block proves charging creates debtors, not neighbors. Open racks avoid the social collapse and the administrative burnout.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I’m voting for Shared Racks. The display frame is manageable, and open access avoids the billing burnout and social debt that plagued the neighbor’s block.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
